-- title:
--   Truncated logarithm covectors are additive modulo p
-- statement:
--   Let $\mathcal O$ be a commutative ring and $p$ a prime with $p$ a non-zero-divisor in $\mathcal O$, equipped with an $\mathcal O$-algebra structure on $\mathbb Z/p$ whose structure map has kernel $(p)$, and assume $\mathcal O$ is $(p)$-adically complete. Let $F$ be a $d$-dimensional commutative multivariate formal group law over $\mathcal O$ (a family `F.toPowerSeries` of $d$ series in $2d$ variables with zero constant term, linear part $X_{\mathrm{inl}\,j}+X_{\mathrm{inr}\,j}$, associative and symmetric under swapping the two blocks). Let $F_p$ be a family of $d$ series in $2d$ variables with zero constant terms satisfying $(F_p)_i$-coefficient at $m\neq 0$ times $p$ equal to $p^{\deg m}$ times the corresponding coefficient of $F_i$, and let $\varphi$ be a family of $d$ series in $d$ variables with zero constant terms, linear part the identity matrix, coefficients tending to $0$ $p$-adically (for each $N$, all but finitely many lie in $(p^N)$), and satisfying $\varphi_i\circ F_p=\varphi_i(X_{\mathrm{inl}})+\varphi_i(X_{\mathrm{inr}})$. Fix $v\in\mathbb N$ and a commutative ring $R$ that is a Hopf algebra over $\mathcal O$, free and finite as $\mathcal O$-module, with $R$ and $R\otimes_{\mathcal O}R$ both $(p)$-adically complete. Let $\pi:\mathcal O[[X_1,\dots,X_d]]\to R$ be a surjective $\mathcal O$-algebra map such that each $\pi(X_i)$ lies in the radical of $(p)R$, such that $\pi$ is computed by $(p)$-adic evaluation at the points $\pi(X_i)$, whose kernel is generated by the components of the $p^v$-division series `F.nthSeries (p ^ v)` (defined by $0$ at step $0$ and by substituting the previous stage into $F$), and such that the comultiplication of $R$ sends $\pi(X_i)$ to the $(p)$-adic evaluation of $F_i$ at $(\pi(X_j)\otimes 1,\,1\otimes\pi(X_j))$. Assume finally that the $\mathbb Z/p$-linear dual of $\mathbb Z/p\otimes_{\mathcal O}R$ is a local ring. Then there is $N_0$ such that for every $N\ge N_0$, every $i$, and every function $c$ on multidegrees with $c(m)=p^{N-\deg m}\cdot\operatorname{coeff}_m\varphi_i$ when $\deg m\le N$ and, when $\deg m>N$, either $c(m)\cdot p^{\deg m-N}=\operatorname{coeff}_m\varphi_i$ or else $c(m)=0$ and $p^{\deg m-N}\nmid\operatorname{coeff}_m\varphi_i$, the following holds: for every Witt vector $\ell\in W(\mathcal O[[X_1,\dots,X_d]])$ whose ghost components satisfy $\operatorname{coeff}_{m'}(\mathrm{gh}_n\ell)=c(p^{N-1-n}m')$ for all $n<N$ and all $m'$, the length-$N$ truncation of the image of $\ell$ under $\pi$ followed by $R\to\mathbb Z/p\otimes_{\mathcal O}R$ lies in [`Deformation.wittHom`](def/Dieudonne_WittVectorHom.html#L246), i.e. its image under $W_N$ of the comultiplication of $A=\mathbb Z/p\otimes_{\mathcal O}R$ equals the sum of its images under $W_N$ of the two inclusions $A\to A\otimes_{\mathbb Z/p}A$.
--
--   This is the finite-level additivity statement underlying Fontaine's description of the Dieudonné module of a smooth commutative formal group by logarithm covectors: the truncated Witt vector built from the rescaled logarithm $\varphi$ becomes a homomorphism of group schemes only after reduction modulo $p$ and modulo the $p^v$-division series, and only for $N$ beyond a threshold. It feeds [`Deformation.exists_wittVector_ghostComponent_truncate_map_mem_wittHom_fontaineKer_of_mvFormalGroup`](thm.html#Deformation.exists_wittVector_ghostComponent_truncate_map_mem_wittHom_fontaineKer_of_mvFormalGroup), which produces the corresponding elements of the Dieudonné module of the $p^v$-torsion of $F$ modulo $p$.
